# d4-snp-tob schedule: 3 holder states x 5 opcodes, one line per cell.
# Rows: UD = dirty TIP (MW agent1), UC = clean TIP (MR agent1),
#       SC+ = client0 holds Branch after LD (directory TRUNK).
# Opcodes: 01 SnpShared, 02 SnpClean, 03 SnpOnce, 04 SnpNotSharedDirty,
#          08 SnpCleanShared. rts=1 only where data return is plausible
#          (dirty holder x data-capable opcode).
# Cycle units: model cycles (dispatcher checks sim_time/20). Measured
# (first pass): phase 1 drains by model ~585, filler window model
# 586-760, sim ends model ~771. Dues 600-740 sit inside the filler.
# Expected responses (selftest-measured baseline): dirty holder answers
# SnpRespData (PassDirty), clean answers SnpResp with post-snoop state,
# SC+ rows must probe l1d (SourceB) before answering.
600 4000 01 1    # UD x SnpShared rts -> SnpRespData PD
610 4040 02 0    # UD x SnpClean
620 4080 03 1    # UD x SnpOnce rts -> SnpRespData PD
630 40c0 04 0    # UD x SnpNotSharedDirty
640 4100 08 0    # UD x SnpCleanShared
650 4140 01 0    # UC x SnpShared -> clean SnpResp
660 4180 02 0    # UC x SnpClean
670 41c0 03 0    # UC x SnpOnce
680 4200 04 0    # UC x SnpNotSharedDirty
690 4240 08 0    # UC x SnpCleanShared
700 4280 01 0    # SC+ x SnpShared -> probe l1d, snpToB family
710 42c0 02 0    # SC+ x SnpClean
720 4300 03 0    # SC+ x SnpOnce
730 4340 04 0    # SC+ x SnpNotSharedDirty
740 4380 08 0    # SC+ x SnpCleanShared -> snpStable family
